From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [mt_wifi7] 066 把「0x01 之后第一个描述符就挂死」拆开看

The HIF reset in 065 is necessary but, measured on the running chip, not
enough: after pulsing it, HIF_BUSY and TX_DMA_BUSY both read zero, and the
next descriptor presented to the download ring sets both again without the
CPU index moving at all.  So the fetch starts and the chip side never takes
the data - the destination is not draining, and because the TX dispatcher
is in order, that one stuck descriptor also kills the command ring that had
been answering seconds earlier.

Two knobs to tell the two remaining explanations apart:

  diag_ram_pre_ms    wait before the first TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ.  The
		     patch has been running for about a hundred milliseconds
		     by then in the failing boots; if its receiver needs
		     longer, a delay alone moves the ring.

  diag_ram_req_only  send the request and push no descriptor at all.  The
		     next region's request then shows whether the MCU came
		     through the request alive - if its index still advances
		     the request is harmless and the descriptor is what
		     hangs the bus.

The 0x05 that downloads the patch in the same window still works, so this
is specific to what runs after PATCH_FINISH_REQ.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -518,6 +518,25 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_skip_ram_req,
 		 "skip TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ and scatter the RAM code directly");
 
+/*
+ * The first descriptor pushed after the patch has taken over never leaves
+ * the FWDL ring: the WFDMA starts the fetch, the chip side never takes the
+ * data, HIF_BUSY sets and from there every TX ring is stuck - the command
+ * ring that answered a moment ago stops as well.  Two ways to narrow it
+ * down without another build: wait longer before the first request, in case
+ * the patch is still bringing its receiver up, and send the request without
+ * any descriptor, which says whether the MCU survives the request itself.
+ */
+static int diag_ram_pre_ms;
+module_param(diag_ram_pre_ms, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_pre_ms,
+		 "wait this long before the first RAM download request");
+
+static bool diag_ram_req_only;
+module_param(diag_ram_req_only, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_req_only,
+		 "send TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ but push no descriptor");
+
 static bool diag_own_retry;
 module_param(diag_own_retry, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_own_retry,
@@ -883,6 +902,13 @@
 		dev_err(dev->dev, "diag: ram sem get -> %d\n",
 			mcu_wm_patch_sem_ctrl(dev, 1));
 
+	if (diag_ram_pre_ms > 0) {
+		dev_err(dev->dev,
+			"diag: waiting %d ms before the first RAM request\n",
+			diag_ram_pre_ms);
+		msleep(diag_ram_pre_ms);
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < hdr->n_region; i++) {
 		const struct mcu_fw_region *region;
 		u32 len = 0, addr = 0, mode = 0;
@@ -972,6 +998,13 @@
 					}
 				}
 
+				if (diag_ram_req_only) {
+					dev_warn(dev->dev,
+						 "diag: request only, no scatter pushed\n");
+					done += part;
+					continue;
+				}
+
 				err = mcu_wm_send_firmware(dev,
 							   data + offset + done,
 							   part);
@@ -1005,6 +1038,13 @@
 				}
 			}
 
+			if (diag_ram_req_only) {
+				dev_warn(dev->dev,
+					 "diag: request only, no scatter pushed\n");
+				offset += len;
+				continue;
+			}
+
 			err = mcu_wm_send_firmware(dev, data + offset, len);
 			if (err) {
 				dev_err(dev->dev, "WM Failed to send firmware\n");
